1
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:07,980
(Song Huan had a car crash?)

2
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:15,160
How did Song Huan suddenly
get into a car accident?

3
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:19,320
Are these all just coincidences?

4
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:22,120
You reap what you sow.

5
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,000
Right?

6
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:25,640
Maybe.

7
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:27,400
Oh, right.

8
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:30,320
Have you noticed lately that

9
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,240
Song Cheng seems off?

10
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:34,880
Like what?

11
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:38,120
I can't quite say.

12
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:40,520
Just a feeling.

13
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:42,120
Maybe you're overthinking it.

14
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:45,000
Look,
Song Huan's been in a car accident,

15
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:46,160
and Song Huaishan's in the hospital.

16
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:48,360
She's got so much on her plate.

17
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:51,800
She's had it rough.

18
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:52,960
Yeah.

19
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:54,640
Maybe.

20
00:00:57,520 --> 00:00:58,160
But...

21
00:00:58,920 --> 00:00:59,720
All right.

22
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:00,800
Don't overthink it.

23
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:01,720
Okay?

24
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:03,320
Look,

25
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:04,200
right now,

26
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:06,240
the biggest obstacle inside Song Group

27
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,240
is gone.

28
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:08,040
In the company,

29
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:10,840
only you and Song Cheng
can call the shots.

30
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:12,960
We must seize this chance.

31
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:14,520
Use Song Cheng

32
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:16,240
to carry out our final plan.

33
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:18,560
You're right.

34
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:23,080
Time to spring the trap.

35
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:29,680
(Song Huan had a car crash?)
(I left a copy of)

36
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:31,760
(A Game of Thrones in my office drawer.)

37
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:34,240
(I left something for you in that book.)

38
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:37,240
(Consider it my last gift to you.)

39
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:41,000
(Given Song Huan's nature,)

40
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,760
(A Game of Thrones, Share Transfer)
(she won't bow out easily.)

41
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:44,960
(She transferred her shares to me)

42
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:47,520
(A Game of Thrones)
(to use me to keep the Songs in check)

43
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:49,360
(Share Transfer Agreement)
(and disrupt the shareholders' meeting.)

44
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:50,410
(Party A - Transferor: Song Huan)
(Power can't rest with one person.)

45
00:01:50,410 --> 00:01:51,560
(Party B - Transferee: Yu Song)
(Power can't rest with one person.)

46
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:54,120
(As a child, Song Huan)

47
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,440
(wasn't as outstanding or kind
as Song Jing)

48
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,560
(nor as sweet and charming as Song Lin.)

49
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:02,280
(Her intense jealousy)

50
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:03,800
(gradually shaped her into)

51
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:05,720
(the obsessive, ruthless woman
she is today.)

52
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,120
(Hateful,)

53
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,720
(yet pitiful.)

54
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:10,920
(But Song Cheng is utterly innocent.)

55
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:14,320
(I can't bear to let others' mistakes)

56
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:16,120
(drag her into this and hurt her.)

57
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:17,920
(Dad.)

58
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,480
(If it were you,)

59
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,080
=Dear Song=
(what would you do?)

60
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:23,180
=Episode 21=
(The Break)

61
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:25,240
Fellow directors,

62
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:27,040
Mr. Song

63
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:28,240
is in recovery.

64
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:31,120
Ms. Song Cheng is the Song family's

65
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,400
only direct descendant.

66
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:33,760
By all rights,

67
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:37,000
she should serve as acting chairwoman

68
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,320
and lead the company.

69
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:39,400
What do

70
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,800
you all think?

71
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:50,520
Everyone,

72
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:53,440
regarding who leads the group,

73
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:54,720
I have something to say.

74
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:01,920
According to current records,

75
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:04,640
I own 12% of Song Group.

76
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:05,520
My stake

77
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:07,200
matches Ms. Song Cheng's.

78
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:20,200
Since even Ms. Song Huan backs her,

79
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:21,120
this woman

80
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,360
must be on her side.

81
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:24,840
Everyone,

82
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,560
Ms. Yu Song's stake

83
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:28,040
matches Ms. Song Cheng's.

84
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:29,120
And her abilities

85
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:30,560
are clear to all.

86
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:31,840
I propose

87
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,280
that Ms. Yu Song

88
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:35,160
take over as chairwoman.

89
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:36,040
Right.

90
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:38,040
Song Group is a listed company.

91
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:39,960
It's about ability and shares.

92
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:42,440
Ms. Yu has worked under
Ms. Song Huan for years.

93
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:44,280
Her ability is beyond doubt.

94
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:45,280
I support her.

95
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:47,160
Song Group

96
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,480
has always passed to direct descendants.

97
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:49,760
Since when

98
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:51,600
does an outsider get to lead?

99
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:52,480
No, no.

100
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:54,120
Ms. Yu Song is far more capable

101
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,400
than the average person.

102
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:57,120
She's just a pawn.

103
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,440
How much of a threat can she really be?

104
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:00,360
Since everyone has doubts,

105
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:02,440
let's settle this by vote.

106
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,000
Fine.

107
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:07,000
Let's have an open showdown.

108
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:09,600
Those for Ms. Song Cheng,

109
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:11,000
raise your hands.

110
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:17,520
Now...

111
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:19,320
Who's for Ms. Yu Song?

112
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:27,160
Even so,

113
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:28,640
Ms. Song Cheng

114
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:30,440
is still a Song.

115
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:32,840
No matter how capable Ms. Yu Song is,

116
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:33,800
in the end,

117
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:35,480
she's still an outsider.

118
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,760
As for Ms. Song Cheng's legs,

119
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:41,800
I'm sure you all know about them.

120
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:44,840
The chair of a company

121
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:46,800
is at the helm.

122
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:50,160
The job requires handling
high-pressure situations frequently.

123
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:51,360
Ms. Song Cheng

124
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:53,560
may not be up to it.

125
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:06,760
If that's what

126
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:09,360
you're all worried about...

127
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:43,760
Then that's no longer a problem.

128
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,480
When did you regain use of your legs?

129
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,840
Not long before you came.

130
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:03,840
After that, it was all an act.

131
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:06,840
I had to pretend to be weak

132
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:09,840
to keep people off guard

133
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:12,680
and survive in the Song family,

134
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:15,760
and see everyone's true colors.

135
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:17,920
You know, Yu Song...

136
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:20,480
After being in a wheelchair so long,

137
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:23,280
I was scared too.

138
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:25,880
What if I could never stand again?

139
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:28,360
So every day

140
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,000
after you left,

141
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:33,560
when everyone was asleep,

142
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:35,600
I'd get up

143
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:37,000
and practice walking.

144
00:06:39,540 --> 00:06:43,880
♪Who leaves whom behind in the past?♪

145
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:45,000
I'd cramp up so badly

146
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,920
that cold sweat

147
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:49,160
soaked through my clothes.

148
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:51,040
And I'd wonder...

149
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:54,600
When would I finally

150
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:57,000
get out of this stupid chair?

151
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,420
♪Sews their tears inside♪

152
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:03,900
♪Love and hate share a seam♪

153
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:06,080
♪Half longing♪

154
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:06,960
Later,

155
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:07,920
♪Half resentment♪

156
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:09,840
there were fewer and fewer people
in my way.

157
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:12,160
So I had more and more time

158
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:15,800
to practice walking.

159
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:18,480
You were the one who taught me

160
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:21,040
how to massage my legs.

161
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:23,560
♪In whose heart are the lies spreading?♪

162
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,360
Yu Song.

163
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:26,840
I've always wondered...

164
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:29,000
♪Half rotting away♪

165
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,240
You're so smart,

166
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,000
so observant.

167
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:36,240
When would you discover my secret?

168
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:40,480
So I always thought I was using you

169
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,560
to clear my path.

170
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:44,560
But actually, you used me

171
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:46,160
to get rid of Song Huan

172
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:48,240
and bring Song Huaishan down.

173
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:50,640
Weren't you using me all along too?

174
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:52,640
We were each other's pawns.

175
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:54,760
So we're even.

176
00:07:58,240 --> 00:07:59,560
When did it start?

177
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:01,960
From...

178
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:04,880
the moment I first saw you

179
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:08,200
and chose you.

180
00:08:10,020 --> 00:08:12,300
♪She stole the moonlight♪

181
00:08:12,540 --> 00:08:14,700
♪Took away the daydreams♪

182
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:15,680
(Ms. Chen.)

183
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:17,560
(I think she's good.)

184
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:19,780
♪Leaving one heart in pain♪

185
00:08:19,980 --> 00:08:21,040
♪No more getting hurt♪

186
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:21,520
Dad.

187
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:23,560
I really like Yu Song.

188
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,880
Since Cheng likes her,

189
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:27,000
Ms. Yu Song can stay.

190
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:30,360
You hurt me on purpose, didn't you?

191
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:32,440
You two are getting out of line.

192
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:34,560
Come with me!

193
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:37,280
Don't cry, Ms. Song Cheng.

194
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:38,560
I'm fine.

195
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:39,240
Really.

196
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:44,460
♪In whose heart are the lies spreading?♪

197
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:46,940
♪Half is a promise♪

198
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:49,560
♪Half rotting away♪

199
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:50,880
(I'll always be here for you.)

200
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:53,640
♪If love always hides something♪

201
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:55,160
To get into the Song family,

202
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:58,640
you needed to back me,
a nobody in the Song family.

203
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,400
And I needed you

204
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:03,080
to gain a foothold in the Song family.

205
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:06,040
We needed each other.

206
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:09,040
I'm not your only pawn, am I?

207
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:12,360
Those shareholders aren't doing this
out of charity.

208
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:13,920
Why do you think

209
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:15,960
they support me?

210
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:19,200
Under every wood carving I gave them,

211
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:23,240
I hid valuable
pre-IPO share certificates.

212
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:25,080
It's a gift of art.

213
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:28,040
And Song Huaishan's stroke.

214
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,440
Do you think

215
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:32,840
Song Huan really caused his stroke?

216
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:37,280
I switched his medicine

217
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:41,320
for look-alike vitamins long ago.

218
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:44,200
I increased the dose bit by bit.

219
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:47,160
He seemed fine most of the time,

220
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:49,760
but whenever he got worked up,

221
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:52,080
you'd hear a pop,

222
00:09:53,040 --> 00:09:53,880
and his blood vessels would burst.

223
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:03,960
Yu Song.

224
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:09,400
You have no right to
look at me like that.

225
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:11,800
What's your relationship with Jing?

226
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:13,240
Your resume,

227
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:15,640
your background,

228
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:17,600
the reason you joined my family.

229
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:19,400
Was any of it true?

230
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:22,440
Yes.

231
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:25,360
I lied to you.

232
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:28,760
We're even.

233
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:34,280
Yu Song, listen.

234
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:36,360
I must take back Song Group.

235
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:41,640
It was mine to begin with.

236
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,880
Back then, Song Huaishan

237
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:46,840
was just a poor student
taken in by my grandpa.

238
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:49,880
My mother pitied him,

239
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:51,480
paid for his schooling,

240
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:52,560
brought him into the Lin family

241
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:53,880
and into the company.

242
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:56,160
He married into the Lin family,

243
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:59,080
yet cheated with another woman

244
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:01,160
and drove my mother to her death.

245
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:03,960
He even told everyone

246
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:06,400
that my mother was the other woman.

247
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:08,440
The Lin family's empire

248
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:10,560
became his Song Group.

249
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:13,280
It was built on my mother's death

250
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:16,200
and all the humiliation I've endured.

251
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,040
Yu Song.

252
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:20,960
Now that you know,

253
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:25,680
will you still fight me for Song Group?

254
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:31,480
Do we...

255
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:34,520
really have to be enemies?

256
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:44,440
Sorry, Song Cheng.

257
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:48,360
I have to take Song Group

258
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:50,240
and destroy it.

259
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:52,960
Because Song Huaishan's empire

260
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:54,840
isn't stained only
with your mother's blood.

261
00:11:56,280 --> 00:11:57,240
Half of it

262
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,440
is stained with my father's blood.
